20% of 20 students is 20/100 * 20 = 4 student. That means 20-4 = 16 students remain. 25% of the remaining (16) students enrolled in jazz dance, this is 25/100 * 16 = 4 students. Thus, 16-4 = 12 students enrolled in hip-hop dance. To find the percentage of students enrolled in hip-hop dance: 12/20 * 100% = 60%.

Therefore, 60% of the entire class enrolled in hip-hop dance.

\boxed{60}

