Each dog takes 0.5 hours per day to care for. Since John takes care of 10 dogs, the total time spent caring for all dogs each day is 10 dogs * 0.5 hours/dog = 5 hours.

There are 7 days in a week. Therefore, the total time spent caring for dogs in a week is 5 hours/day * 7 days/week = 35 hours.

\boxed{35}

